				<title>The Mad Poker Genius Who Disappeared for 20 Years | PokerNews Podcast #1012</title>
				<link>https://www.pokernews.com/video/the-mad-poker-genius-who-disappeared-for-20-years-pokernews-13511.htm?utm_medium=feed&amp;utm_campaign=homefeed&amp;utm_source=rss</link>
				<pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 07:43:50 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.pokernews.com/video/the-mad-poker-genius-who-disappeared-for-20-years-pokernews-13511.htm?utm_medium=feed&amp;utm_campaign=homefeed&amp;utm_source=rss</guid>

				
				

				
					<description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://i.ytimg.com/vi/rTVahHP_WzA/mqdefault.jpg" alt="" style="padding:5px;" /></p><p>The legendary poker player disappeared from the poker world 20 years ago, and Chad managed to track him down for an exclusive two-part interview. In Part I, Caro talks about his early days in poker, mastering poker tells, and some of his famous laws such as &quot;The Law of Least Tilt&quot; and the &quot;Threshold of Misery.&quot;

Caro then discusses some of his poker books, including writing Super System alongside his good friend and longtime confidant Doyle Brunson. A forerunner in the world of poker technology, Caro also shares details about his early computer program ORAC, signing on with the first-ever online poker site, Planet Poker, and being an ambassador for Doyle&#039;s Room.

Part II of Mike Caro&#039;s interview will air at 8 a.m. PT/11 a.m. ET on Thursday, October 29, so be sure to tune in then.</p>]]></description>
				
				
			</item><item>
